# Advisor note #14 — External human anchor for v2 location and severity (MAPLEZ gold + IU MeSH)

**Date:** 2026-10-13 · **Phase:** Tier 1 closeout → Tier 2 gate
**Builds on:** #13 (closeout checklist), D45 (schema v2 = the four MAPLEZ fields), `d3` §8.3 (E5,
RadGraph-XL). **Proposed IDs:** E5.1 (MAPLEZ gold) and E5.2 (IU MeSH). Renumber if they collide.

**Why this note exists.** Every v2 `location` and `severity` number so far compares the student
with the teacher. Nobody has measured whether the **v2 teacher** gets location and severity right.
Tier 2 trains on those targets, so a systematic teacher error, for example a left/right flip,
would carry forward silently. Two public human references cost about one GPU-hour and close
that gap for chest. Non-chest anatomies have no public reference and stay with the reader study
(W6).

