## 5. Pre-registered readings. Commit this table before computing

| Result (clean categories, MIMIC, limited vocabulary) | Reading | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Location F1 ≥ 0.80 **and** flip rate ≤ 2% | v2 teacher location is at MAPLEZ level | v2 location targets are cleared for Tier 2. Record it in DECISIONS |
| Location F1 0.65–0.80, or flip rate 2–5% | Usable with a caveat | Break errors down by category and type: missing granularity (mild) vs wrong lobe vs wrong side. Tier 2 proceeds, and the readout carries the caveat |
| Location F1 < 0.65, or flip rate > 5% | **Teacher location is not trustworthy** | **Stop before Tier-2 joint training.** Owner decides between a prompt rule fix plus a targeted re-label of location only, or dropping location from the training loss. Do not regenerate silently |
| Severity binary F1 < 0.60 | The severity field is mostly noise | Strengthens D45's drop rule. It does **not** replace E4.2, which still decides |
| Clean-category presence > 10pp below the MAPLEZ reference | Probably a definitional difference (taxonomy split, history rule). Possibly a teacher gap | List the top 10 disagreement types (**no report text**). Compare with the pilot-set root causes in `v3/pilot-test-set/` |
| R2: student−teacher agreement with gold within ±2pp (paired CI includes 0) | Fidelity carries over to external human agreement | This is the paper sentence: the student inherits teacher quality on external human labels |

